course: dictionary
lesson: 838
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word bent is a good example. Its main meaning is not straight: «A straw in water looks bent» means the straw seems curved or folded where it meets the water.
explain: Bent can also be the past form of bend. «He bent the wire» means he curved the wire in the past. The verb forms are bend, bends, bent and bending. If the sentence tells you about something that already happened, bent is probably the past tense.
explain: Bent is also part of phrases. «The soldiers were bent double» means they bent over so far that their bodies folded in half. Bent on means very determined to do something. Always check: does your meaning still make sense when you put it into the sentence?
fact: Bent means not straight any more: curved or folded. A bent spoon or bent nail is damaged.
fact: Bent is the past form of bend: «He bent the wire» means he curved it.
fact: «Bent on» means very determined to do something.
fact: In science, light bends: «A straw in water looks bent» because light changes direction as it passes from water into air.
fact: In British slang, bent can mean dishonest, so check the context carefully when you meet it.
exercise: «A straw in water looks bent.» What does bent mean here? | *Not straight, curved or folded | Past tense of bend, as in he bent something | Dishonest | Very determined
exercise: «Her brother is bent on winning the race.» What does bent on mean? | *Very determined to do something | Sleeping | Curved over | Lost
exercise: Which word fills the gap in «He ___ the wire into a hook yesterday.»? | *bent | bends | bend | bending
test: «The soldiers were bent double to pass under the arches.» What does bent double mean? | Standing very tall | Lying on the ground asleep | *Bent over so far that they folded in half | Wearing a hat
test: What does bent mean in «The bike wheel was bent after the crash»? | Dishonest | *Damaged and no longer straight | Very determined | Past tense of bend, meaning someone bent it
exam: Mia says bent always means dishonest. Is she right? | No, it can mean curved, the past tense of bend, or very determined | Yes, bent always means dishonest | Yes, but only in science lessons | *No, it has several meanings, so check the context
